re not stored in the table, this should be interpreted as"32 different signals with a signal code > 1".If a signal is caught, the signal handler is not reset to.ulSIG_DFLas it is in many flavors of UNIX(tm)..endtopic.topic RETURN VALUE.ulsignal()returns the address of the old signal handler for this signal. If the signalnumber was 0,.ulsignal()returns the address of the old default signal handler for unknown signals.If the signal number was 1, a 0 is returned without any further action.If the signal table is full,.ulsignal()returns -1 without any further action..endtopic.topic EXAMPLES.noform#include <signal.h>void sig_hand(int sig){/* handle SIGINT ... */   \.   \.}void other_sigs(int sig){/* will be called for all signals except SIGQUIT and SIGINT !! */  \.  \.}signal(SIGINT,sig_hand);     /* special function for SIGINT */signal(SIGQUIT,SIG_IGN);     /* ignore SIGQUIT */signal(0,other_sigs);        /* default-signal handler */.noformend.endtopic